# .trivyignore — Python image
# Format: CVE-ID  [expiry-date]  # reason
#
# Add accepted/deferred CVEs here with a justification comment and optional
# expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD). Entries without an expiry must be reviewed
# quarterly. Never suppress CRITICAL CVEs without an approved exception.
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-XXXXX 2025-06-01 # false-positive in unused component; upstream fix pending

# libncursesw6 / libtinfo6 / ncurses-base — buffer overflow in ncurses.
# No fix released for Debian as of 2026-04-08. ncurses is a terminal
# library; this container runs a headless HTTP server with no terminal
# interaction, so the vulnerable code path is not reachable.
CVE-2025-69720

# libsystemd0 / libudev1 — arbitrary code execution / DoS in systemd.
# No fix released for Debian as of 2026-04-08. libsystemd0 is pulled
# in as a transitive dependency; the container does not use systemd
# services or the journald API.
CVE-2026-29111
